": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Acme Supplies"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The wire went through even though the call timed out, but the invoice is still marked approved. Linking the payment to the invoice instead of paying again:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GNF2oiWTRVtriuuA4sEBek", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"payment_id": "PAY0001", "invoice_id": "INV-14684"}, "name": "link_payment", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I paid Acme Supplies's approved invoice once, by wire, and it's now marked paid.\n\n**Payment:** PAY0001, $4,377.10 wire from the operating account to Acme Supplies (vendor V-979), status \"sent.\"\n**Invoice:** INV-14684, due 2026-11-04, now marked **paid**.\n\nThe wire request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the payments list and found the wire had actually gone out. The invoice still showed as unpaid, though, so I recorded PAY0001 against it rather than sending a second payment. There are no duplicate payments.\n\nThis was under the $10,000 limit, so it didn't need controller approval. Acme's other invoices were left alone: INV-45616 ($5,848.07) is still a draft waiting for approval, and INV-70059 was already paid.", "type": "text"}]}]}